EXPERIMENT 54 – FILE UPLOAD AUTOMATION USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate the file upload functionality of a website.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Create a temporary text file using File.createTempFile().
3. Write a line into the file.
4. Open the file upload page.
5. Send the absolute file path to the file input element using sendKeys().
6. Click the Upload button.
7. Read the upload status and uploaded file name.
8. Verify the status and file name.
9. Close the browser.
CODE
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import java.io.File;
import java.nio.file.Files;

public class Exercise54 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            File file = File.createTempFile("upload_", ".txt");

            Files.writeString(file.toPath(),
                "Selenium file upload test");

            driver.get(
                "https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/upload");

            driver.findElement(By.id("file-upload"))
                .sendKeys(file.getAbsolutePath());

            driver.findElement(By.id("file-submit")).click();

            String status = driver.findElement(
                By.tagName("h3")).getText();

            String uploaded = driver.findElement(
                By.id("uploaded-files")).getText();

            System.out.println("Upload status     : " + status);
            System.out.println("File name matches : "
                + uploaded.equals(file.getName()));

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- URL: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/upload
- File: Temporary .txt file
- Content: Selenium file upload test
OUTPUT
Upload status     : File Uploaded!
File name matches : true


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to automate file upload functionality was executed successfully, and the output was verified.
